-#### Particle Splatting for Density Field Construction
-A 3D density field representing a wax surface is constructed on the CPU every frame by splatting interpolated particles into a 3D grid aligned with the container [S19, unofficial]. Temporal smoothing is applied in-place using the update rule: $keep = \text{exp}(-dt/\tau)$, where $\tau = 0.04$ seconds [S19, unofficial]. Grid dimensions are 48×94×48 voxels, aligned with the container [S19, unofficial]. The kernel is a separable kernel defined as $(1 - u^2)^3$ [S19, unofficial]. Two channels are stored per voxel: (1) density, (2) temperature × density [S19, unofficial]. Density is normalized to approximately 1 at the core of the wax [S19, unofficial]. GPU Texture Format is Data3DTexture with RG channel layout [S19, unofficial]. Internal format is RG32F (float32), or RG16F if the GPU does not support filtering of 32-bit floats [S19, unofficial]. CPU splatting takes 1.1 to 1.25 ms median, and 1.3 to 1.9 ms p95, measured on a Xeon 2.1 GHz processor [S19, unofficial].
