-Triangulates the polygon.
+### Differentiable Rendering (Forward Pass)
+For each pixel $j$ with polar coordinates $(\rho_j, \theta_j)$ in the tangent plane of primitive $s_i$, compute signed distance to boundary: $\varphi_j = \rho_j - r_i(\theta_j)$ [S26]. Discard points with $\varphi_j \ge 0$ (outside primitive). Compute per-pixel opacity: $\alpha_{i,j} = o_i \cdot \max\left(0, \frac{r_i(\theta_j) - \rho_j}{r_i(\theta_j)}\right)^{\sigma_i}$ [S26]. Accumulate colors via front-to-back compositing [S26].
 
-#### Differentiable Forward Warping with Average Splatting
-A warping strategy that estimates deformation from canonical time to another time step, ensuring smooth flows. It uses average splatting to handle the many-to-one issue where multiple source positions map to one target position [S27, unofficial]. The formula is $\Vgrid {}{T}[\mathbf {p}] = \frac {\sum _{\forall \mathbf {q}\in \Vgrid {}{S}}b[\mathbf {u}]\cdot \Vgrid {}{S}[\mathbf {q}]}{\sum _{\forall \mathbf {q}\in \Vgrid {}{S}}^{}b[\mathbf {u}]}$, where $b[\mathbf {u}] = \prod \text {max}(0, 1\!-\!\left |\mathbf {u}_i \right |), {i} \in \{x,y,z\}$, and $\mathbf {u} = (\mathbf {q}+f_{\text {S}\rightarrow \text {T}}[\mathbf {q}]) - \mathbf {p}$. $x, y, z$ are three axes of the voxel grid, and $u_i \in \mathbb {R}$ is one element of the vector $\mathbf {u} \in \mathbb {R}^3$ [S27, unofficial]. The many-to-one issue: Multiple positions in the source correspond to the same position in the target (e.g., when a circle shrinks). This is handled by average splatting which fuses multiple values into one using a trilinear kernel [S27, unofficial].
+### 3D Splatting
+A rendering technique used to generate volume-sampled tools on-the-fly for interactive sculpting operations (specifically 'sawing'), preventing object space aliasing while achieving interactive speed [S27, unofficial]. It generates the volume-sampled tool on-the-fly using a user interface [S27, unofficial]. It renders the generated tool using 3D splatting to prevent aliasing and maintain interactive frame rates [S27, unofficial].
 
